Z||000000||reddog||11-01-2001||07:52 PM||||I was considering buying Tomco injectors and the bigbore throttle body from the fiero store. Has anyone used these products and if so what was the results? Also can this be done and still use the factory ecm?<P>1986 GT 2.8l V6 Auto(5speed in 2weeks)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||11-01-2001||08:15 PM||||I have both, but I also have the lower temp fan switch, thermostat, and chip from the Fiero store. The car runs alot cooler and richer to the point that I just ordered the thermostat and fan switch from Rodney Dickman to see if I could get it to run a little more normal (leaner). Otherwise the car runs great and feels very powerful.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||reddog||11-01-2001||08:32 PM||||Avengador1 was the difference very noticable from stock? low end ,mid-range, high end, what did it help most?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||voyagerspe||11-01-2001||09:56 PM||||I use the "bigbore" on my 3.4 in my 87 gt<BR>I think it works well im not really sure if you would feel the difference "in the seat of your pants"  as for the injectors I use mustang injectors MUCH cheaper (get them off ebay)||||reg||7
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||11-02-2001||12:42 AM||||The Tomco injectors are good but you'd be better off using a bored out t-body and upper plenum from Darrel Morse.<BR>He charges $150.00 to bore out your t-body and the upper plenum that it hooks to so you'll get more power. That price also includes return shipping and the gasket.<BR>His work is excellent and you won't be disappointed, there's a lot of forum members that have Darrels products on their cars and are very happy with the results, myself included. <BR>You can get in touch with Darrel via email at<BR>morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||reddog||11-02-2001||12:49 AM||||Whats the turn around on the tb and plenium work?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-02-2001||10:24 AM||||Darrel is fast... he often times has extra plenums already finished and just takes yours as a core.  I've got his TB & Intake, as well as his Strut tower brace.  He's an awsome guy to work with!||||reg||1
Z||000007||avengador1||11-02-2001||11:12 AM||||I notice the difference above 2000 RPM, thats were it starts to come on strong all the way to 6000 RPM's.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||slik88gt||11-02-2001||12:18 PM||||Also check out the Heartland Fiero Club, they offer a bored out throttle body, upper plenum and lower plenum at an extremly reasonable price. They also offer a upper plenum that has been modified to allow for more volume then just boring out can offer, they do this by mounting a custom polished or chrome air box on the top of the plenum, and for character this air box can be engraved to exactly match the factory "fiero" engraving in the plenum....  ||||reg||1
